<!-- <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/main.css"> -->

    <title>MetaROR - MetaResearch Open Review</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #ffffff;
            color: #333;
            overflow-x: hidden; /* Prevent horizontal scrolling */
        }
        .container {
            width: 100%;
            max-width: 1200px;
            margin: 1em auto;
            padding: 10px;
            text-align: center;
            box-sizing: border-box; /* Include padding and border in element's total width and height */
        }
        .header {
            background-color: #e8f4ff;
            padding: 40px 20px;
            margin: 0 0 1em 0;
            text-align: center;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .header img {
            max-width: 80%;
            min-width: 40%;
            height: auto;
        }
        .announcement {
            font-size: 28px;
            color: #2C71B4;
            margin: 1em 0 0 0;
        }
        .intro {
            font-size: 16px;
            line-height: 1.6;
            margin: 0 10% 2em 10%;
        }
        .steps {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            justify-content: center;
            margin: 2em 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .step {
            background-color: #e8f4ff;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 8px;
            padding: 20px;
            margin: 1em;
            flex: 1 1 30%;
            box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
            box-sizing: border-box;
            min-width: 280px; /* Ensure steps have a minimum width */
        }
        .step img {
            max-width: 100%;
            height: auto;
            margin-bottom: 1em;
        }
        .step h2 {
            margin-top: 0.5em;
        }
        .footer {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            align-items: center;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            margin: 3em 0;
        }
        .footer img {
            max-width: 250px;
            min-width: 80px;
            max-height: 120px;
            min-height: 50px;
            margin: 2em;
            flex: 1;
        }
        .subscribe {
            background-color: #2C71B4;
            color: #ffffff;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 1em 0;
            text-align: center;
        }
        .subscribe input {
            padding: 10px;
            margin: 1em 0;
            width: calc(100% - 22px);
            max-width: 500px;
            border: none;
            border-radius: 4px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        .subscribe button {
            background-color: #ffffff;
            color: #2C71B4;
            padding: 10px 20px;
            border: 2px solid #2C71B4;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
            margin: 10px 0;
        }
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .steps {
                flex-direction: column;
                align-items: center;
            }
            .step {
                flex: 1 1 100%;
            }
            .footer img {
                max-width: 250px;
                max-height: 60px;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="header">
        <img src="/assets/images/metaror-blue-back.svg" alt="MetaROR - MetaResearch Open Review">
        <div class="announcement">Coming in November 2024</div>
    </div>
    <div class="container">
  <script>
  const myArray = {{ article | dump | safe }};
  console.log(myArray);
  </script>

    <div class="intro">
            <h1>Introducing MetaROR - MetaResearch Open Review</h1>
            <p>MetaROR is a collaborative initiative led jointly by the Research on Research Institute (RoRI) and the Association for Interdisciplinary Meta-Research and Open Science (AIMOS), which are working together to build a platform to leverage the strengths of the Publish - Review - Curate approach for the various metaresearch disciplines.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
            <div class="step">
                <img src="/assets/images/img-publish.jpg" alt="Publish">
                <h2>Publish</h2>
                <p>This initial step involves the researcher submitting a preprint to a repository where it can be accessed by peers and the public. This step is crucial for early dissemination of research and can facilitate broader feedback and collaboration.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <img src="/assets/images/img-review.jpg" alt="Review">
                <h2>Review</h2>
                <p>During this phase, reviewers can provide feedback, critiques, and suggestions. This peer review is conducted openly, with reviews being visible to the public and becoming a part of the knowledge creation process.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="step">
                <img src="/assets/images/img-curate.jpg" alt="Curate">
                <h2>Curate</h2>
                <p>Editors assess the reviews and the preprint, providing an editorial assessment to contextualize the feedback and quality of the work. This step adds a layer of validation to the research, so that high standards are maintained.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="footer">
            <a href="https://researchonresearch.org/"><img src="/assets/images/logo-rori.jpg" alt="Research on Research Institute"></a>
            <a href="https://aimos.community/"><img src="/assets/images/aimos.png" alt="Association for Interdisciplinary Meta-Research and Open Science"></a>
        </div>
        <div class="subscribe">
            <h2>Be the first to know!</h2>
            <p>Register your email to keep updated about the launch and relevant developments</p>    

<div id="mc_embed_signup">
